/*--- Choupo stream state.  Every DIMENSIONAL value carries its unit; the parser converts to SI.
     componentMolarFlows is the OVERALL material (all phases); a phases{} block, when present,
     is a decomposition that sums back to it exactly. ---*/

componentMolarFlows
{
    NH3    10 kmol/h;
    N2    90 kmol/h;
}

//  PHASE PIN (2026-08-14).  This stream is the case's gas feed -- the header
//  says so: "Feed gas: 100 kmol/h, 10 % NH3 / 90 % N2".  The pin states that
//  fact, and it is what the engine's own state writer emits for a vapour
//  holding a SUB-CRITICAL species (StreamStateIO: a permanent gas is
//  recovered by the Tc screen and needs none, which is why stripper01's
//  pure-N2 feed is correct without one; NH3 at 298 K is below its Tc, so the
//  phase must be declared).  This file was hand-authored and missed it.
//
//  What the pin was worth here: the energy report was pricing the stream as
//  a LIQUID, putting 55 kW of phantom enthalpy into the column's balance
//  (dH read +82.93 kW against +27.98).  That the ABSENCE of a pin has that
//  effect is an ENGINE defect, not this file's -- the reader states plainly
//  that the 0.0 default is "a starting value" and that "consumers that price
//  energy ask phasePinned, never vf == 0", and the energy report asks vf.
//  Recorded as DEV.md 4b V2; this pin is correct on its own merits either
//  way, because the stream really is a gas.
phase           gas;
T               298.15 K;
P               101325 Pa;
